// Title: Suspicious Scheduled Task Creation Involving Temp Folder
// Sigma ID: 39019a4e-317f-4ce3-ae63-309a8c6b53c5
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-03-11 | Modified: 2022-10-09
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, execution, persistence, T1053.005
// Description: Detects the creation of scheduled tasks that involves a temporary folder and runs only once
// False positives:
//   - Administrative activity
//   - Software installation
// References:
//   - https://discuss.elastic.co/t/detection-and-response-for-hafnium-activity/266289/3
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_schtasks_creation_temp_folder.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\schtasks.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " /create " and ProcessCommandLine contains " /sc once " and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Temp\\")
